    "question": {
        "text": "§\n\nOther than D2 receptors, what receptors do first generation antipsychotics inhibit?",
        "imageIds": []
    },
    "answer": {
        "text": "§\nOther than D2 receptors, what receptors do first generation antipsychotics inhibit?\n\n(1) Muscarinic receptors\n(2) α1 receptors\n\n(3) H1 receptors\n\n(Note: this occurs predominantly in the LOW potency first generation antipsychotics)\n\n[Image: dc9785dcadc307501a271035aba21c0ec38814f9453e06205ccfbb9262dc49a3]\n\n[Image: 63363167bcca489ba9747c41f5d0c5779483c77ec563ad20ead5ca531ad2895a]\n\n[Image: 6b955c00b35ba4c366bc0b33f92ea8456377497ff5c2816d29c6be30c93c4558]\n\n5.1 - First generation antipsychotics\n[Image: 200ef1c009b3b266b3583f9b4d9e10fb1caa8940070d0b905749a3474112cf5f]\n\n[Image: d8214ad280ce2cc641eacc7e93ad25f9b6e0c7f1ea8c5a9f5cae2be4561b73fb]\n\n[Image: 44444e5c55bab9d789789b80ffeb27d73b29ad3770e9b09e1768fe78a62993ce]",
